		}
		{
			title: "ADVENT CRAFTS"
			x: -2.25d
			y: -2.75d
			shape: "square"
			description: [
				"&dHey Bandit, while you are out and about gathering the things for this teleporter, you might want to keep raising your skills as well. "
				""
				"&dThese skills are going to be important for finding materials for crafting."
				""
				"&dKeep chopping trees, hunting monsters, mining stone and ore, and even fishing and running around and stuff."
				""
				"&dThe Advent of Ascension stuff isn't locked behind DLC thankfully. Weapons and armor are locked behind Project MMO levels, though, but we don't have to worry about that for a bit."
			]
			dependencies: ["5FC0C65E68336246"]
			id: "5F43029723C5AA50"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6685150EA4FFB28A"
				type: "checkmark"
				title: "Advent Crafting - Overworld"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Tea Time"
			x: -2.25d
			y: -5.0d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Calming"
			description: [
				"&dTea is one of those things that can make the world slow down for a moment so you can enjoy a cuppa. "
				""
				"&dAdvent of Ascension has its own interesting Tea system. You'll need to make a Tea Sink, which is a setup to brew tea. You place it out, Right Click a Bucket of Water onto it to fill it, then Right Click ingredients and a Cup onto it to brew Tea."
				""
				"&dTo make a Cup, you'll need to find Ivory from some of the Advent monsters. The Chomper can be found in Swamps in the Overworld, for example."
				""
				"&dTea Seeds can be drop from any hostile mob, or from chopping down trees if your Logging is at Level 10+."
				""
				"&dSimple Tea is made by making sure the Teasink has Water, then Right Click the Tea Shreddings onto the Teasink, then the Cup. "
			]
